              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-41722-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-41722 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A path traversal vulnerability exists in filepath.Clean on Windows.\n\nOn Windows, the filepath.Clean function could transform an invalid path such as \"a/../c:/b\" into the valid path \"c:\\b\". This transformation of a relative (if invalid) path into an absolute path could enable a directory traversal attack.\n\nAfter fix, the filepath.Clean function transforms this path into the relative (but still invalid) path \".\\c:\\b\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/57274",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-41722\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.19.6,1.20.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2022-41722](https://go.dev/issue/57274)",
