            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-24536-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-24536 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Multipart form parsing can consume large amounts of CPU and memory when processing form inputs containing very large numbers of parts.\n\nThis stems from several causes:\n\n1. mime/multipart.Reader.ReadForm limits the total memory a parsed multipart form can consume. ReadForm can undercount the amount of memory consumed, leading it to accept larger inputs than intended.\n2. Limiting total memory does not account for increased pressure on the garbage collector from large numbers of small allocations in forms with many parts.\n3. ReadForm can allocate a large number of short-lived buffers, further increasing pressure on the garbage collector.\n\nThe combination of these factors can permit an attacker to cause an program that parses multipart forms to consume large amounts of CPU and memory, potentially resulting in a denial of service. This affects programs that use mime/multipart.Reader.ReadForm, as well as form parsing in the net/http package with the Request methods FormFile, FormValue, ParseMultipartForm, and PostFormValue.\n\nWith fix, ReadForm now does a better job of estimating the memory consumption of parsed forms, and performs many fewer short-lived allocations.\n\nIn addition, the fixed mime/multipart.Reader imposes the following limits on the size of parsed forms:\n\n1. Forms parsed with ReadForm may contain no more than 1000 parts. This limit may be adjusted with the environment variable GODEBUG=multipartmaxparts=.\n2. Form parts parsed with NextPart and NextRawPart may contain no more than 10,000 header fields. In addition, forms parsed with ReadForm may contain no more than 10,000 header fields across all parts. This limit may be adjusted with the environment variable GODEBUG=multipartmaxheaders=."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/59153",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-24536\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.19.8,1.20.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2023-24536](https://go.dev/issue/59153)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-24536**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.19.8,1.20.3  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2023-24536](https://go.dev/issue/59153)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45287-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45287 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Before Go 1.20, the RSA based TLS key exchanges used the math/big library, which is not constant time. RSA blinding was applied to prevent timing attacks, but analysis shows this may not have been fully effective. In particular it appears as if the removal of PKCS#1 padding may leak timing information, which in turn could be used to recover session key bits.\n\nIn Go 1.20, the crypto/tls library switched to a fully constant time RSA implementation, which we do not believe exhibits any timing side channels."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/20654",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45287\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.20.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2023-45287](https://go.dev/issue/20654)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45287**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.20.0  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2023-45287](https://go.dev/issue/20654)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-68121-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-68121 critical vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During session resumption in crypto/tls, if the underlying Config has its ClientCAs or RootCAs fields mutated between the initial handshake and the resumed handshake, the resumed handshake may succeed when it should have failed. This may happen when a user calls Config.Clone and mutates the returned Config, or uses Config.GetConfigForClient. This can cause a client to resume a session with a server that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake, or cause a server to resume a session with a client that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/K09ubi9FQFk",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-68121\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.24.13,1.25.7,1.26.0-rc.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2025-68121](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/K09ubi9FQFk)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-68121**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.24.13,1.25.7,1.26.0-rc.3  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2025-68121](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/K09ubi9FQFk)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "10.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-41724-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-41724 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Large handshake records may cause panics in crypto/tls.\n\nBoth clients and servers may send large TLS handshake records which cause servers and clients, respectively, to panic when attempting to construct responses.\n\nThis affects all TLS 1.3 clients, TLS 1.2 clients which explicitly enable session resumption (by setting Config.ClientSessionCache to a non-nil value), and TLS 1.3 servers which request client certificates (by setting Config.ClientAuth \u003e= RequestClientCert)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/58001",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-41724\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.19.6,1.20.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2022-41724](https://go.dev/issue/58001)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-41724**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.19.6,1.20.1  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2022-41724](https://go.dev/issue/58001)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29409-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29409 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Extremely large RSA keys in certificate chains can cause a client/server to expend significant CPU time verifying signatures.\n\nWith fix, the size of RSA keys transmitted during handshakes is restricted to \u003c= 8192 bits.\n\nBased on a survey of publicly trusted RSA keys, there are currently only three certificates in circulation with keys larger than this, and all three appear to be test certificates that are not actively deployed. It is possible there are larger keys in use in private PKIs, but we target the web PKI, so causing breakage here in the interests of increasing the default safety of users of crypto/tls seems reasonable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/61460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-29409\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.19.12,1.20.7,1.21.0-rc.4\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2023-29409](https://go.dev/issue/61460)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-29409**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.19.12,1.20.7,1.21.0-rc.4  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2023-29409](https://go.dev/issue/61460)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78663-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78663 critical vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/847187",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78663\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nVersion: v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110\nFix Version: 0.60.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-78663](https://go.dev/cl/847187)",
