                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97032-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97032 high vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP/2 servers could end up crashing due to inadvertently modifying its HPACK encoder concurrently. This happens because the server modifies the HPACK encoder from two goroutines without synchronization: one uses the encoder to encode a HEADERS frame as part of a response sent to a client and the other modifies the encoder's table size when handling a SETTINGS frame containing SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE that a client sends. A malicious client can repeatedly send a request while changing the header table size to crash the server."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/847188",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97032\nSeverity: high\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nVersion: v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110\nFix Version: 0.60.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-97032](https://go.dev/cl/847188)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97032**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | golang.org/x/net  | v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110  | 0.60.0  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-97032](https://go.dev/cl/847188)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
