              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97030 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A trusted template author may have previously written a valid template wherein the use of the 'yield' keyword would not be correctly escaped.\n\nWe now ensure that valid keyword uses are escaped and non-keyword uses are not escaped."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/840925",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97030\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.9,1.27.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-97030](https://go.dev/cl/840925)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97030**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.26.9,1.27.2  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-97030](https://go.dev/cl/840925)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97054-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97054 low vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "For HTTP/1 servers, when MaxBytesReader's limit is exceeded, \"Connection: close\" header is automatically set without synchronization, which might race with another header being set explicitly in the server handler. As a result, an HTTP/1 server that utilizes MaxBytesReader or MaxBytesHandler can crash due to runtime panic if its handler reads the request body concurrently with writing the response header."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/862185",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97054\nSeverity: low\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.11,1.27.4\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-97054](https://go.dev/cl/862185)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97054**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.26.11,1.27.4  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-97054](https://go.dev/cl/862185)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27139-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27139 low vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened.\n\nThe impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/EdhZqrQ98hk",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27139\nSeverity: low\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.25.8,1.26.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-27139](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/EdhZqrQ98hk)",
